From bb03c1965785a32466ef43f594a8dd2ffad25472 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 18:34:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 33/38] WIP mmb: A-panel double-buffered GLU tile (IQ3_S) --
 the dequant overlaps WMMA

mmb_tile_gemm / mmb_tile_gemm_glu gain DBUF: the next K-step's weight dequant
writes the other A buffer (As/Ag/Au 2x, Bs single) so it overlaps the current
step's WMMA instead of serializing behind the single-buffer barrier hazard.

Measured on Flash-Next IQ4_XS (the IQ3_S GLU, 96 calls, fixed prompt):
routed_glu<64,32,16,16,5> 1018.8 -> 942.0 ms (-7.5 %), mrg total 1318 -> 1229
(-6.7 %), MMB family -2.6 %, total GPU kernel time -1.8 %.

Enabled ONLY for WTYPE 5 (IQ3_S): DBUF regresses Q4_K (+5.8 % on the 35B GLU,
287 -> 304 ms) and the dense Q8_0 tile (+37 %), so it stays off there.  The
35B is bit-identical/unchanged with this build (mrg 287.3 vs 287.4 ms).

DBUF2 (also double-buffer B -> one sync per K-step) is MEASURED REFUTED
(mrg 1225 -> 1433 ms) and is kept guarded, disabled.

Bit-identical: PPL c2048 10.6015, greedy sha 9c281c415082, width probe PASS.
